.Dd November 6, 2026
.Dt GSSD 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm gssd
.Nd establish RPCSEC_GSS contexts for the NFS server
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl d
.Op Fl h Ar hostname
.Op Fl k Ar keytab
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
accepts Kerberos V5 contexts for the kernel's NFS server, which then
handles every message of those contexts itself.
It needs the key of
.Li nfs/ Ns Ar hostname
in the keytab.
It also maps principals to local users.
.Pp
A principal
.Li user@REALM
of the default realm is the local user of that name.
.Li host/ Ns Ar name ,
.Li nfs/ Ns Ar name
and
.Li root/ Ns Ar name
are root, to which the export's
.Fl maproot
applies.
Any other principal is the export's anonymous user.
.Pp
The options are:
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Fl d
Stay in the foreground and log to standard error.
.It Fl h Ar hostname
The host name of the service principal, by default
.Xr gethostname 3 .
.It Fl k Ar keytab
The keytab.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width /var/run/gssd.sock -compact
.It Pa /var/run/gssd.sock
the socket the kernel connects to
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr exports 5 ,
.Xr mountd 8
.Sh STANDARDS
.Rs
.%R RFC 2203
.%T RPCSEC_GSS Protocol Specification
.Re
